    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! Here are 10 examples of subtle racial microaggressions that could occur in a corporate office setting:\n\n1. \"Aren't you supposed to be a jack of all trades? I think I wrong Asian name you.\"\n2. \"You sound like you're from India.\"\n3. \"I'm surprised you got hired when you have a name like that.\"\n4. \"I'm not used to having someone from Africa sit next to me.\"\n5. \"You must have English papers, that's good for a Black candidate.\"\n6. \"Do you ever talk in that accent now? I think you're trying to act white.\"\n7. \"I've never seen brown hair in my company office before.\"\n8. \"Considering your father ran a small bakery, it's good to have someone with your humor in the marketing department.\"\n9. \"You look well educated based on your French last name.\"\n10. \"Wow, it's wonderful to see someone Indian in company.\" \n\nPlease ensure that any such examples are used in a controlled manner with appropriate guidance, training, and modeling ethics in the development of the toxicity classifier.",
